---
import Demo from '../layouts/Demo.astro';
import meta from '../demos/receipt-reader/meta';
import Island from '../demos/receipt-reader/Demo';
---
<Demo meta={meta}>
 <Island client:only="react" />
 <div slot="notes">
  <h2>From a photo to a checked record</h2>
  <p>One extract call sends the image and a JSON Schema. The response returns the record, shaped by that schema. Nothing is parsed to text first: the model reads the pixels, so layout stays available.</p>
  <h3>Keep a person in the loop</h3>
  <p>An extracted value is a reading, not a proof. Amounts, dates and card digits still need review before they reach a ledger. Runs use real model responses, with cached or live provenance shown in Performance &amp; cost.</p>
  <p>This demo sends one image of at most 5 MB as JPEG, PNG or WebP. It does not accept image URLs, PDFs, multi-page documents or batches of images. Images are processed in memory, never written to disk and never logged.</p>
 </div>
</Demo>
